              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for to pull, then the Kannada for to cry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಯಾರೂ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯಾರೂ — yārū — \"nobody (with a negative verb)\". Kannada negates a verb by joining ಇಲ್ಲ (illa) onto it: ಯಾರೂ ಬರಲಿಲ್ಲ — yārū baralilla — \"Nobody came.\" ಇಲ್ಲ also means \"is not there\"; to say something is not a thing, it uses ಅಲ್ಲ (alla): ಇದು ನನ್ನ ಮನೆ ಅಲ್ಲ — idu nanna mane alla — \"This is not my house.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯಾರೂ (yārū) is native Dravidian: yāru, \"who\" (DEDR 5151), with -ū, \"even\": with a \"not\" verb, \"not even anyone\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
