        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಯಾರಾದರೂ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯಾರಾದರೂ — yārādarū — \"anyone, someone\". A yes-or-no question changes the last vowel of the sentence's final word to -ಆ (-ā): ಇದ್ದಾರೆ becomes ಯಾರಾದರೂ ಇದ್ದಾರಾ? — yārādarū iddārā? — \"Is anyone there?\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯಾರಾದರೂ (yārādarū) is native Dravidian: yāru, \"who\" (DEDR 5151), and ādarū, \"even if it is\", from āgu, \"to become\" (DEDR 333): \"whoever it may be\". DEDR 333 compares Sanskrit ām."
            }
          ]
        },
